                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 1260.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Protocol of the meeting field at the German legation
                        on February 21, 1891</hi>.</head>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <item>Present: The representatives of Belgium, France, the German Empire, Great
                        Britain, Italy, Japan, the Netherlands, Russia, Spain, and the United
                        States.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Mr. von Brandt having read the annexed memorandum of his interview with the
                    ministers of the yamên on the 19th instant, his action was approved. After a
                    short discussion the annexed programme of the rules to be observed at the
                    audiences and general receptions was approved, and Mr. von Brandt was authorized
                    to place it before the ministers of the yamên at their next meeting as the
                    unanimous expression of opinion of the foreign representatives to be embodied in
                    the final protocol to be signed by the Chinese ministers and foreign
                    representatives. The meeting then separated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. von Brandt</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
